{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>On the palms of Aaron, and he shall wave.</b> Both are engaged in the waving — the owners and the priest. How so? The priest places his hand beneath the hand of the owners and waves. And in this case Aaron and his sons were the owners, and Moses was the priest." "<b>Wave-offering.</b> He moves it out and in — to Him whose are the four winds of the world; the wave-offering stays and cancels punishments and evil winds; he raises and lowers — to Him whose are the heavens and the earth, and it stays harmful dews (Menachot 62)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:35.389343241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}